{%- comment -%}
  sections/ds-product-main.liquid — Disrupted Studio custom PDP

  Replaces Horizon's `product-information` section entirely. Renders the
  full hero (breadcrumb + 7:5 grid of gallery left, info column right)
  with everything brutalist-styled and editable per-product via standard
  product fields + metafields. NO quantity selector. NO theme blocks —
  this section owns all of its content.

  ---
  DATA SOURCES
  ---

  PRODUCT FIELDS (Shopify built-in, no setup needed):
    product.title              → big H1 title
    product.type               → eyebrow caps text (e.g. "Photoshop Plugin")
    product.price              → main price (mono)
    product.compare_at_price   → strikethrough + auto LAUNCH -X% tag
    product.description        → long description below the form
    product.media              → gallery main + thumbnails
    product.collections        → first non-trivial collection = breadcrumb

  PRODUCT METAFIELDS (namespace: "disrupted", optional, per-product):
    badge_text       (string)                   → orange badge text (e.g. "NEW · v1.0"); hidden if blank
    tagline          (string)                   → short paragraph under the title
    demo_url         (url)                      → sub-CTA link destination (label is sub_cta_label)
    sub_cta_label    (string)                   → text on the sub-CTA link. Defaults to "Watch the demo"
                                                  for plugins; set to "See the full specimen" for fonts, etc.
    plugin_specs     (Plugin specs metaobject)   → typed plugin spec rows:
                                                   compat, format, file_size, license, updates, support
    font_specs       (Font specs metaobject)     → typed font spec rows:
                                                   family, glyphs, formats, language, license
    graphics_specs   (Graphics specs metaobject) → typed graphics spec rows:
                                                   items, formats, resolution, license, updates
    specs            (list of Spec metaobjects)  → generic fallback for unusual product types.
                                                   Each Spec has `label` + `value` text fields.

  Spec rendering priority:
    plugin_specs → font_specs → graphics_specs → specs (list) → legacy keys.
  First non-empty set wins. Section hides if all are empty.

  DEPRECATED (still works if set, lowest priority):
    compat / format / file_size / license / updates / support — old flat
    metafield keys. Use plugin_specs metaobject instead going forward.

  All metafields are OPTIONAL. Rows without a value just don't render.
  See docs/changes.md for the metafield definition setup steps.

  ---
  NOTES
  ---
  - Form submits natively (page reload). Phase 5 polish can upgrade to
    Horizon's <product-form-component> for AJAX + cart-drawer integration.
  - Variant picker is a simple <select> for multi-variant products; hidden
    for single-variant. Selected variant's ID is what the form posts.
  - Thumb-swap uses ~15 lines of vanilla JS at the bottom, scoped to this
    section. Respects prefers-reduced-motion via CSS.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign cs = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1'

  comment
    Breadcrumb: prefer the product's first non-"all"/"frontpage" collection.
  endcomment
  assign crumb_collection = nil
  for c in product.collections
    if c.handle != 'all' and c.handle != 'frontpage'
      assign crumb_collection = c
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Eyebrow: product.type, fall back to crumb collection title.
  endcomment
  assign eyebrow_text = product.type
  if eyebrow_text == blank and crumb_collection
    assign eyebrow_text = crumb_collection.title
  endif

  comment
    Badge: fully merchant-editable via the disrupted.badge_text metafield.
    Type anything ("NEW · v1.0", "BESTSELLER", "LIMITED"), or leave blank
    to hide entirely. No tag-based logic — explicit content control.
  endcomment
  assign badge_text = product.metafields.disrupted.badge_text.value

  comment
    Sale calc.
  endcomment
  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign saved = product.compare_at_price | minus: product.price
    assign discount_percent = saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price | round
  endif

  comment
    Optional content metafields.
  endcomment
  assign tagline = product.metafields.disrupted.tagline.value
  assign sub_cta_label = product.metafields.disrupted.sub_cta_label.value | default: 'Watch the demo'

  comment
    demo_url: URL-scheme allowlist.  Only http(s):// absolute URLs and
    same-origin paths (starting with `/` or `#`) are honoured.  Anything
    else (e.g. a stray `javascript:` URI in a metafield) is treated as
    blank so the sub-CTA hides entirely.  Defence-in-depth — the
    metafield is merchant-controlled, but allow lists are cheap.
  endcomment
  assign raw_demo_url = product.metafields.disrupted.demo_url.value
  assign demo_url = ''
  if raw_demo_url != blank
    if raw_demo_url contains '://'
      if raw_demo_url contains 'http://' or raw_demo_url contains 'https://'
        assign demo_url = raw_demo_url
      endif
    else
      assign first_char = raw_demo_url | slice: 0, 1
      if first_char == '/' or first_char == '#'
        assign demo_url = raw_demo_url
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Specs — resolved in priority order:
    1. plugin_specs metaobject  (Compat/Format/File size/License/Updates/Support)
    2. font_specs metaobject    (Family/Glyphs/Formats/Language/License)
    3. graphics_specs metaobject (Items/Formats/Resolution/License/Updates)
    4. specs (list of generic Spec metaobjects, free label+value)
    5. legacy flat keys (backward compat)
  endcomment
  assign plugin_specs   = product.metafields.disrupted.plugin_specs.value
  assign font_specs     = product.metafields.disrupted.font_specs.value
  assign graphics_specs = product.metafields.disrupted.graphics_specs.value
  assign specs_list     = product.metafields.disrupted.specs.value

  assign legacy_spec_keys   = 'compat,format,file_size,license,updates,support' | split: ','
  assign legacy_spec_labels = 'Compat,Format,File size,License,Updates,Support' | split: ','

  assign has_specs = false
  if plugin_specs or font_specs or graphics_specs
    assign has_specs = true
  elsif specs_list and specs_list.size > 0
    assign has_specs = true
  else
    for key in legacy_spec_keys
      assign v = product.metafields.disrupted[key].value
      if v != blank
        assign has_specs = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

<section class="ds-pdp color-{{ cs }}">
  <div class="ds-pdp__inner">

    {%- comment -%} ----- BREADCRUMB ----- {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="ds-pdp__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="ds-pdp__crumb-link">Home</a>
      <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- if crumb_collection -%}
        <a href="{{ crumb_collection.url }}" class="ds-pdp__crumb-link">{{ crumb_collection.title }}</a>
        <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="ds-pdp__crumb-current">{{ product.title }}</span>
    </nav>

    {%- comment -%} ----- HERO ----- {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ds-pdp__hero">

      {%- comment -%} ----- GALLERY ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ds-pdp__gallery">
        <div class="ds-pdp__gallery-main">
          {%- if product.featured_media -%}
            {{
              product.featured_media.preview_image
              | image_url: width: 1600
              | image_tag:
                loading: 'eager',
                fetchpriority: 'high',
                widths: '600,900,1200,1600',
                sizes: '(min-width: 900px) 56vw, 100vw',
                alt: product.title,
                class: 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img',
                id: 'ds-pdp-main-img-' | append: section.id
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'ds-pdp__gallery-main-img placeholder-svg' }}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Inset prev/next arrows — overlay the hero image, only rendered
            when more than one media item exists.  Wired up by the existing
            gallery script at the bottom of this section; arrow click =
            cycle to the prev/next thumbnail with wrap-around at ends.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="ds-pdp__gallery-nav ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev"
              data-ds-gallery-prev
              aria-label="Previous image"
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="ds-pdp__gallery-nav ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next"
              data-ds-gallery-next
              aria-label="Next image"
            >
              <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs">
            {%- for media in product.media limit: 8 -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="ds-pdp__gallery-thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
                data-src="{{ media | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
                aria-label="View image {{ forloop.index }}"
              >
                {{
                  media.preview_image
                  | image_url: width: 200
                  | image_tag:
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    alt: '',
                    class: 'ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-img'
                }}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ----- INFO COLUMN ----- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ds-pdp__info">

        {%- comment -%}
          EYEBROW + OPTIONAL BADGE.  All four sources here are
          merchant-controlled text — Shopify Liquid doesn't auto-
          escape `{{ }}` output, so we explicitly | escape any
          metafield-driven text to be safe against a stray HTML/JS
          paste into the metafield value.  Defense in depth.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if eyebrow_text != blank or badge_text != blank -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-eyebrow">
            {%- if eyebrow_text != blank -%}
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-cat">{{ eyebrow_text | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if badge_text != blank -%}
              <span class="ds-pdp__info-badge">{{ badge_text | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} TITLE — product.title is sanitised by Shopify, no escape needed {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="ds-pdp__info-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>

        {%- comment -%} TAGLINE (metafield) {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if tagline != blank -%}
          <p class="ds-pdp__info-tagline">{{ tagline | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} PRICE ROW (price + compare-at + sale tag inline) {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="ds-pdp__info-price-row">
          <span class="ds-pdp__info-price">{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
          {%- if on_sale -%}
            <span class="ds-pdp__info-price-strike">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</span>
            <span class="ds-pdp__info-sale-tag">Launch −{{ discount_percent }}%</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          BUY FORM (ATC, no quantity)

          Wrapped in Horizon's <product-form-component> so the submit is
          intercepted, posted to /cart/add.js via AJAX, and a CartAddEvent
          is dispatched. The cart-drawer-component listens for that event
          and (because it has `auto-open`) slides itself open with the new
          item already inside — no full page reload.

          Required wiring:
            data-section-id          — for cart morphing
            data-product-id          — for analytics + variant events
            on:submit="/handleSubmit" — declarative intercept
            ref="liveRegion"         — SR announcement target (required)
            ref="variantId"          — current variant input (required)

          Variant products: the user-facing <select> drives a hidden
          <input name="id" ref="variantId"> that the component reads. A
          tiny inline listener keeps the two in sync on change.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script src="{{ 'product-form.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>

        <product-form-component
          data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
          data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
          on:submit="/handleSubmit"
          class="ds-pdp__info-form-component"
        >
          <div
            class="visually-hidden"
            aria-live="assertive"
            role="status"
            aria-atomic="true"
            ref="liveRegion"
          ></div>

          {%- form 'product', product, class: 'ds-pdp__info-form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Hidden input is always the one product-form-component reads.
              For variant products the visible <select> writes into it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input
              type="hidden"
              name="id"
              ref="variantId"
              value="{{ current_variant.id }}"
              data-ds-variant-input
            >
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">

            {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
              <div class="ds-pdp__info-variant">
                <label class="ds-pdp__info-variant-label" for="ds-variant-{{ section.id }}">
                  {{ product.options.first | default: 'Variant' }}
                </label>
                <select
                  id="ds-variant-{{ section.id }}"
                  class="ds-pdp__info-variant-select"
                  data-ds-variant-select
                >
                  {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                    <option
                      value="{{ variant.id }}"
                      {% if variant.id == current_variant.id %}selected{% endif %}
                      {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                    >
                      {{ variant.title }} — {{ variant.price | money }}{% unless variant.available %} (sold out){% endunless %}
                    </option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endunless -%}

            <button
              type="submit"
              name="add"
              class="ds-btn ds-btn--lg ds-btn--full ds-pdp__info-cta"
              data-ds-main-atc
              {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
            >
              {%- if current_variant.available -%}
                Add to cart — {{ current_variant.price | money }}
              {%- else -%}
                Sold out
              {%- endif -%}
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
        </product-form-component>

        {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Tiny per-section script: keep the hidden variantId input in sync
            with the user-facing variant select so AJAX submits the right id.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <script>
            (function () {
              var sec = document.getElementById('shopify-section-{{ section.id }}');
              if (!sec) return;
              var select = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-select]');
              var hidden = sec.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-input]');
              if (!select || !hidden) return;
              select.addEventListener('change', function () {
                hidden.value = select.value;
              });
            })();
          </script>
        {%- endunless -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          SUB-CTA (metafield demo_url).  `demo_url` was scheme-allowlisted
          above (http/https/`/`/`#` only); | escape on the href as a
          belt-and-braces attribute escape.  Same for sub_cta_label.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if demo_url != blank -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-sub-cta">
            <a href="{{ demo_url | escape }}" class="ds-text-link">
              {{ sub_cta_label | escape }}
              <span class="ds-text-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} SPECS TABLE — typed sets (plugin/font/graphics) preferred, then generic, then legacy {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_specs -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-specs">
            {%- if plugin_specs -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.compat.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Compat</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.compat.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.format.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Format</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.format.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.file_size.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">File size</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.file_size.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.license.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.license.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.updates.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Updates</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.updates.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if plugin_specs.support.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Support</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ plugin_specs.support.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif font_specs -%}
              {%- if font_specs.family.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Family</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.family.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.glyphs.value   != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Glyphs</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.glyphs.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.formats.value  != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Formats</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.formats.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.language.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Language</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.language.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if font_specs.license.value  != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ font_specs.license.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif graphics_specs -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.items.value      != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Items</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.items.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.formats.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Formats</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.formats.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.resolution.value != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Resolution</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.resolution.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.license.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">License</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.license.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if graphics_specs.updates.value    != blank -%}<div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">Updates</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ graphics_specs.updates.value | escape }}</span></div>{%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif specs_list and specs_list.size > 0 -%}
              {%- for spec in specs_list -%}
                {%- assign label = spec.label.value -%}
                {%- assign value = spec.value.value -%}
                {%- if label != blank and value != blank -%}
                  <div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">{{ label | escape }}</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ value | escape }}</span></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- for key in legacy_spec_keys -%}
                {%- assign value = product.metafields.disrupted[key].value -%}
                {%- if value != blank -%}
                  <div class="ds-pdp__info-spec"><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-label">{{ legacy_spec_labels[forloop.index0] }}</span><span class="ds-pdp__info-spec-value">{{ value | escape }}</span></div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} LONG DESCRIPTION {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.description != blank -%}
          <div class="ds-pdp__info-description">
            {{ product.description }}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  ----- STICKY ADD-TO-CART BAR -----
  Appears at the top of the viewport once the user has scrolled past
  the main buybox, so the conversion path is always visible while
  reading features, FAQs, video, etc.

  Anatomy
    [ thumb 48px ] [ name + price ] [ + ADD TO CART ]

  Implementation
    • Lives OUTSIDE the main <section> so it's a sibling element with
      simple position:fixed positioning relative to viewport.
    • Hidden by default. JS adds `.is-visible` when the main ATC's
      bottom edge has scrolled above the header.
    • Wrapped in <product-form-component> so submitting it triggers
      AJAX add + opens the cart drawer (same flow as the main ATC).
    • Variant + price stay in sync with the main form via small JS
      bridge (listens for change on the variant select).
{%- endcomment -%}
<product-form-component
  class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta"
  data-ds-sticky-cta
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  on:submit="/handleSubmit"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <div class="visually-hidden" aria-live="assertive" role="status" aria-atomic="true" ref="liveRegion"></div>
  <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner">

    {%- comment -%} thumb (links to top of page) {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="#" class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media" aria-label="Back to top" data-ds-sticky-top>
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        {{
          product.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 120
          | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              alt: product.title,
              widths: '48,96,144',
              sizes: '48px',
              class: 'ds-pdp-sticky-cta__img'
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    {%- comment -%} name + price stack {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__info">
      <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name">{{ product.title }}</div>
      <div class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price" data-ds-sticky-price>
        {%- if current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price -%}
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price-strike">{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ current_variant.price | money }}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ATC form — own product-form-component instance {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- form 'product', product, novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="id"
        ref="variantId"
        value="{{ current_variant.id }}"
        data-ds-sticky-variant
      >
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      <button
        type="submit"
        name="add"
        class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn"
        {% unless current_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
      >
        {%- if current_variant.available -%}
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label">Add</span>
          <span class="ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long">Add to cart</span>
        {%- else -%}
          Sold out
        {%- endif -%}
      </button>
    {%- endform -%}
  </div>
</product-form-component>

{% style %}
  /* ds-pdp — port of mockup .pdp-* (lines 1528-1660) with ds- namespace */

  .ds-pdp {
    background: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
  .ds-pdp__inner {
    padding-left: var(--pad-x);
    padding-right: var(--pad-x);
  }

  /* Breadcrumb */
  .ds-pdp__crumb {
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-link {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-link:hover { color: var(--color-fg); }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-sep { opacity: 0.4; }
  .ds-pdp__crumb-current { color: var(--color-fg); }

  /* Hero grid: 7fr gallery, 5fr info */
  .ds-pdp__hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7fr 5fr;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-9);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ds-pdp__hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-7);
    }
  }

  /* Gallery */
  .ds-pdp__gallery {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main .placeholder-svg {
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: var(--space-7);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     GALLERY NAV ARROWS
     Small prev/next buttons overlaid on the hero image.  Only
     render when product.media.size > 1.  Sit inside the existing
     `.ds-pdp__gallery-main` (position: relative), so the absolute
     positioning is local to the square image frame.
     Brutalist treatment: sharp corners, mono glyph, semi-opaque
     dark background, hover lifts opacity + accent border.
     ============================================================ */
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    padding: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45);
    border-radius: 0;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    z-index: 2;
    opacity: 0.65;
    transition:
      opacity var(--t-fast) var(--ease),
      background var(--t-fast) var(--ease),
      border-color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-main:hover .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav:hover,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav:focus-visible {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    opacity: 1;
    outline: none;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev { left: 12px; }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next { right: 12px; }

  /* Touch devices: arrows always at full opacity (no hover state to reveal them). */
  @media (hover: none) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav { opacity: 0.85; }
  }

  /* Mobile: slightly smaller + tighter inset so they don't crowd the image. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav {
      width: 32px;
      height: 32px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--prev { left: 8px; }
    .ds-pdp__gallery-nav--next { right: 8px; }
  }

  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb {
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    overflow: hidden;
    cursor: pointer;
    position: relative;
    transition: border-color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
    padding: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb:hover,
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb.is-active {
    border-color: var(--color-fg);
  }
  .ds-pdp__gallery-thumb-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Info column — sticky on desktop */
  .ds-pdp__info {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height, 64px) + var(--space-4));
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ds-pdp__info { position: static; }
  }

  /* Eyebrow + NEW badge row */
  .ds-pdp__info-eyebrow {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-cat {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--fs-caps);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    /* Brutalist outlined chip — thin grey border, no fill, sharp corners */
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 0;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 7px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent-fg);
  }

  /* Title */
  .ds-pdp__info-title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 0.9;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Tagline */
  .ds-pdp__info-tagline {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 32ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Price row */
  .ds-pdp__info-price-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-price {
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-price-strike {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-sale-tag {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-sale);
    padding: 3px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-sale);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  /* Form */
  .ds-pdp__info-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-micro);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-select {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    color: var(--color-fg);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    border-radius: 0;
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    /* Caret arrow */
    background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, currentColor 50%),
                      linear-gradient(135deg, currentColor 50%, transparent 50%);
    background-position: calc(100% - 20px) 50%, calc(100% - 14px) 50%;
    background-size: 6px 6px, 6px 6px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    padding-right: 36px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-variant-select:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-cta:disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  /* Sub-CTA */
  .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta {
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Specs */
  .ds-pdp__info-specs {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-label {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-spec-value {
    color: var(--color-fg);
    text-align: right;
  }

  /* Long description */
  .ds-pdp__info-description {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  .ds-pdp__info-description p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .ds-pdp__info-description strong { color: var(--color-fg); font-weight: 500; }
  .ds-pdp__info-description ul,
  .ds-pdp__info-description ol {
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp__info-description li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }

  /* -------------------------------------------------------------------
     Mobile (≤600px) — phone-specific tightening
     ------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    /* Title can scale down a touch on tightest screens */
    .ds-pdp__info-title { font-size: clamp(30px, 9vw, 48px); }

    /* Price shrinks slightly so it doesn't dwarf everything */
    .ds-pdp__info-price { font-size: 24px; }
    .ds-pdp__info-price-strike { font-size: 16px; }

    /* Tagline tightens its line length on narrow */
    .ds-pdp__info-tagline { font-size: 16px; max-width: none; }

    /* Gallery thumbs — keep 4 across, just tighten the gap so squares
       breathe more on narrow screens */
    .ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs { gap: var(--space-2); }

    /* Specs — long values were colliding with labels in the flex layout.
       Stack label above value with a small gap on mobile. */
    .ds-pdp__info-spec {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 4px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
    }
    .ds-pdp__info-spec-value { text-align: left; }

    /* Sub-CTA gets a bigger tap target on touch */
    .ds-pdp__info-sub-cta a { padding: 6px 0; display: inline-block; }
  }

  /* ============================================================
     STICKY ADD-TO-CART BAR
     Fixed at top, slides down once the main ATC scrolls out of view.
     Sits below the sticky header so the header nav stays accessible.
     ============================================================ */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta {
    position: fixed;
    /* --ds-search-top tracks the live bottom edge of the header (set by
       JS in ds-header.liquid). This accounts for the announce bar +
       sticky header state. Falls back to header height. */
    top: var(--ds-search-top, var(--header-height, 64px));
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 45;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-fg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    transform: translateY(-110%);
    transition:
      transform  var(--t-base, 240ms) var(--ease, cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)),
      visibility var(--t-base, 240ms) var(--ease, cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1));
    visibility: hidden;
    /* Reset inherited form layout */
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta.is-visible {
    transform: translateY(0);
    visibility: visible;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--pad-x);
    max-width: 1600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    min-height: 64px;
  }

  /* Thumbnail — click to scroll back to top */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media {
    display: block;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: var(--color-bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Name + price */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__info {
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    font-feature-settings: "tnum";
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price-strike {
    text-decoration: line-through;
    color: var(--color-fg-faint);
    margin-right: 6px;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* ATC button — mono caps brutalist */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn {
    background: var(--color-fg);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: background var(--t-fast) var(--ease), color var(--t-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent-fg);
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-icon {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  /* Show short "Add" on phones, full "Add to cart" on bigger screens */
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label { display: inline; }
  .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 500px) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label { display: none; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn-label-long { display: inline; }
  }

  /* Mobile — tighter padding, smaller thumb */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      min-height: 56px;
    }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__media { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__name { font-size: 13px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__price { font-size: 12px; }
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta__btn { padding: 10px 14px; }
  }

  /* Reduced motion: drop the slide, just toggle visibility */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ds-pdp-sticky-cta { transition: none; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Disrupted PDP main",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ds-section ds-section--pdp-main",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1",
      "label": "Color scheme"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Disrupted PDP main"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

<script>
  // Gallery — thumbnail swap + inset prev/next arrow nav
  //
  // Scopes everything to the nearest `.ds-pdp__gallery` so multiple
  // galleries on a page (shouldn't happen on PDP but safe) don't
  // collide.  The `activate(btn)` helper is the single source of
  // truth: thumbnail click and arrow click both funnel through it,
  // so the active state + main-image swap stay consistent.
  //
  // Arrows wrap at ends (prev from index 0 jumps to the last image,
  // next from the last image jumps back to 0).
  (function () {
    document.querySelectorAll('.ds-pdp__gallery').forEach(function (gallery) {
      var mainImg = gallery.querySelector('.ds-pdp__gallery-main-img');
      var thumbs  = gallery.querySelector('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumbs');
      if (!mainImg || !thumbs) return;

      var thumbList = Array.prototype.slice.call(
        thumbs.querySelectorAll('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumb'));

      function activate(btn) {
        if (!btn) return;
        var src = btn.getAttribute('data-src');
        if (!src) return;
        thumbList.forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-active'); });
        btn.classList.add('is-active');
        // Wipe responsive attrs so the browser actually loads our explicit src
        // (otherwise srcset can win and you see the original featured image)
        mainImg.removeAttribute('srcset');
        mainImg.removeAttribute('sizes');
        mainImg.src = src;
      }

      // Thumbnail click — direct activation.
      thumbs.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var btn = e.target.closest('.ds-pdp__gallery-thumb');
        if (!btn) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        activate(btn);
      });

      // Inset arrow nav — step ±1 through thumbList, wrap at ends.
      function step(delta) {
        if (thumbList.length === 0) return;
        var currentIdx = thumbList.findIndex(function (b) {
          return b.classList.contains('is-active');
        });
        if (currentIdx === -1) currentIdx = 0;
        var nextIdx = (currentIdx + delta + thumbList.length) % thumbList.length;
        activate(thumbList[nextIdx]);
      }
      var prevBtn = gallery.querySelector('[data-ds-gallery-prev]');
      var nextBtn = gallery.querySelector('[data-ds-gallery-next]');
      if (prevBtn) {
        prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          step(-1);
        });
      }
      if (nextBtn) {
        nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
          e.preventDefault();
          step(1);
        });
      }
    });
  })();

  // Sub-CTA smooth-scroll — if the demo_url metafield is a #anchor
  // (e.g. "#video", "#features"), intercept the click and smooth-scroll
  // to that PDP section, offset by the sticky header height. Full URLs
  // (https://…, /pages/…) fall through to normal navigation.
  (function () {
    var link = document.querySelector('.ds-pdp__info-sub-cta a');
    if (!link) return;
    var href = link.getAttribute('href') || '';
    if (href.charAt(0) !== '#' || href.length < 2) return;

    link.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var target = document.querySelector(href);
      if (!target) return;
      e.preventDefault();

      // For the type specimen specifically, auto-open the glyph dropdown
      // before scrolling. Otherwise clicking "VIEW FULL SPECIMEN" lands
      // the user on a collapsed accordion and they'd have to click again.
      // FAQ details intentionally stay closed (different UX expectation).
      target.querySelectorAll('details.ds-pdp-typespecimen__details:not([open])').forEach(function (d) {
        d.open = true;
      });

      var header = document.querySelector('.ds-header');
      var offset = (header ? header.offsetHeight : 64) + 16;
      var y = target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - offset;
      window.scrollTo({ top: y, behavior: 'smooth' });
    });
  })();

  // Sticky ATC bar — show when the main ATC has scrolled above the
  // header, hide when it's back in view. Also sync variant + price
  // between the main form and the sticky form so the right variant
  // is added when the user has picked one.
  (function () {
    var bar       = document.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-cta]');
    var mainAtc   = document.querySelector('[data-ds-main-atc]');
    if (!bar || !mainAtc) return;

    function getHeaderBottom() {
      // Prefer live measurement (announce bar may be in view, or not)
      var hdr = document.querySelector('.ds-header');
      if (hdr) {
        var b = hdr.getBoundingClientRect().bottom;
        if (b > 0) return b;
      }
      // Fallback: read --ds-search-top (updated live by ds-header JS)
      var v = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--ds-search-top');
      var n = parseInt(v, 10);
      if (n > 0) return n;
      // Last resort
      return 64;
    }

    var ticking = false;
    function update() {
      var rect = mainAtc.getBoundingClientRect();
      var threshold = getHeaderBottom();
      // Show once the main ATC's bottom edge has scrolled above the
      // bottom of the sticky header (with a small buffer).
      var shouldShow = rect.bottom < threshold + 4;
      bar.classList.toggle('is-visible', shouldShow);
      bar.setAttribute('aria-hidden', shouldShow ? 'false' : 'true');
      ticking = false;
    }
    function onScrollOrResize() {
      if (!ticking) {
        requestAnimationFrame(update);
        ticking = true;
      }
    }

    update();
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScrollOrResize, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', onScrollOrResize, { passive: true });

    // Click the sticky thumbnail → scroll back to top of the PDP
    var topLink = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-top]');
    if (topLink) {
      topLink.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    }

    // Sync variant + price between the main form and the sticky form
    var mainSelect    = document.querySelector('[data-ds-variant-select]');
    var stickyVariant = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-variant]');
    var stickyPrice   = bar.querySelector('[data-ds-sticky-price]');
    if (mainSelect && stickyVariant) {
      mainSelect.addEventListener('change', function () {
        stickyVariant.value = mainSelect.value;
        // Refresh the visible price too. The variant id matches the
        // option element's value; pull its label which we embed below
        // as "Title — $XX.YY" so we can extract the trailing price.
        var opt = mainSelect.options[mainSelect.selectedIndex];
        if (opt && stickyPrice) {
          var m = opt.textContent.match(/(\$|€|£)\s?[\d.,]+/);
          if (m) stickyPrice.textContent = m[0];
        }
      });
    }
  })();
</script>
